import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Retro: grammar gaps — closing the measured refusals, and the pay wall","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/grammar-gaps.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/grammar-gaps.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/grammar-gaps.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="retro-grammar-gaps-—-closing-the-measured-refusals-and-the-pay-wall" tabindex="-1">Retro: grammar gaps — closing the measured refusals, and the pay wall <a class="header-anchor" href="#retro-grammar-gaps-—-closing-the-measured-refusals-and-the-pay-wall" aria-label="Permalink to “Retro: grammar gaps — closing the measured refusals, and the pay wall”">​</a></h1><p>Date: 2026-10-14 Context: the ADR-0007 layer-2 handler grammar (<code>mlopt_discovery.handler_synth</code>) mints a non-elementwise atom by proposing a descriptor from a structured template vocabulary and verifying it fp64 against the pre-mint spec. The composed loop (<code>lab/mint/atom_synth_loop.py</code>) runs need -&gt; handler -&gt; laws -&gt; admission -&gt; pay. Five refusals were measured; this round closes four and names the fifth precisely.</p><p>Changed code lives in <code>packages/mlopt-discovery/src/mlopt_discovery/handler_synth.py</code> plus its test file; <code>lab/audit/grammar_probe.py</code> is the census instrument. Nothing under <code>mlopt-core</code> changed.</p><h2 id="the-refusals-before-after-mint-verdict-at-budget-512" tabindex="-1">The refusals, before -&gt; after (mint verdict at budget 512) <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-refusals-before-after-mint-verdict-at-budget-512" aria-label="Permalink to “The refusals, before -&gt; after (mint verdict at budget 512)”">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>spec</th><th>before</th><th>after</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>cumsum(X, dim=1)</code> verbatim</td><td>0 candidates</td><td>MINTED <code>(&quot;fold_emit&quot;,1.0,&quot;X&quot;,0.0,&quot;$acc&quot;,-2)</code> tried=3</td></tr><tr><td><code>H0 + cumsum(X, dim=1)</code></td><td>0 candidates</td><td>MINTED <code>(&quot;fold_emit&quot;,1.0,&quot;X&quot;,&quot;H0&quot;,&quot;$acc&quot;,-2)</code> tried=3</td></tr><tr><td><code>sum(X, dim=-1)</code></td><td>0 candidates</td><td>MINTED <code>(&quot;reduce&quot;,&quot;sum&quot;,&quot;X&quot;,-1)</code> tried=35</td></tr><tr><td><code>mean(X, dim=-1)</code></td><td>0 candidates</td><td>MINTED <code>(&quot;reduce&quot;,&quot;mean&quot;,&quot;X&quot;,-1)</code> tried=37</td></tr><tr><td><code>softmax</code></td><td>0 candidates</td><td>MINTED <code>(&quot;norm&quot;,&quot;div&quot;,(&quot;exp&quot;,&quot;X&quot;),&quot;sum&quot;,(&quot;exp&quot;,&quot;X&quot;),-1,True)</code> tried=38</td></tr><tr><td>SelectiveScan verbatim (2 metas)</td><td>512-budget refusal</td><td>MINTED <code>(&quot;fold_emit&quot;,(&quot;sigmoid&quot;,&quot;A&quot;),&quot;B&quot;,0.0,&quot;$acc&quot;,-2)</code> tried=44</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The extensions, each verified through the unchanged fp64 gate:</p><ul><li><strong><code>reduce</code> family</strong> — <code>(&quot;reduce&quot;, op, sub, axis)</code> over sum/mean/prod/amax/amin on the spec&#39;s own <code>dim</code> attrs plus -1/-2.</li><li><strong>identity sides</strong> — an empty fold a/b partition spells its side&#39;s identity (1.0 for a, 0.0 for b); with the scalar-operand lift (<code>_as_tensor</code>, commit 311fac1) these are live again, so a carry-less recurrence is spellable.</li><li><strong>neutral carries</strong> — a fold may start from 0.0/1.0 (<code>FOLD_CARRIES</code>), so a spec with no explicit carry meta reaches its canonical form.</li><li><strong><code>norm</code> family</strong> — <code>(&quot;norm&quot;, op, lhs, red_op, rhs, axis, keepdim)</code>, a value combined with a reduction of (another) value; the composite the <code>reduce</code> family&#39;s whole-spec operand cannot spell.</li></ul><h2 id="the-budget-heuristics-confirmed-not-relaxed" tabindex="-1">The budget heuristics, confirmed not relaxed <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-budget-heuristics-confirmed-not-relaxed" aria-label="Permalink to “The budget heuristics, confirmed not relaxed”">​</a></h2><p>The <code>fold</code>/<code>fold_emit</code> <strong>family</strong> keeps its <code>&gt;= 3</code> meta floor: the one/two-meta mints all come from the <code>fold_emit</code> <strong>seed</strong> (<code>_canonical_emit_seeds</code>), and relaxing the floor only explodes the space — <code>cumsum(X)</code>&#39;s <code>fold_emit</code> column grows from 36 (the seed) to 147700 candidates, a two-meta spec&#39;s from 144 to &gt;200000, every battery spec mints the <em>same</em> body at the <em>same</em> index, and the <code>applyd</code>-nest <code>fold_zip</code> mint regresses out of a 1500 budget.</p><p>The emit projection depth is capped at one non-accumulator op (<code>_MAX_EMIT_OPS</code>): the emitted-scan corpus emit is <code>$acc</code> and the next useful form is one op; a two-op projection is outside the cap.</p><h2 id="dead-space" tabindex="-1">Dead space <a class="header-anchor" href="#dead-space" aria-label="Permalink to “Dead space”">​</a></h2><p>The old dead region (bare-float fold fillers) was already lifted. This round found and removed two more: a <strong>non-<code>keepdim</code> normalization</strong> cannot broadcast its denominator back, and the <strong>both-identity fold</strong> (<code>a=1.0, b=0.0</code>) has no step axis. Measured on the cumsum spec: 143 of the first 600 candidates raised, 141 of them non-keepdim norm bodies; after deriving <code>keepdim</code> off the spec (<code>_spec_keepdim</code>), gating the norm family to normalization-shaped specs, and dropping the both-identity forms, <strong>0 raise</strong>. The residual raises on two-meta specs are shape-incompatible <code>contract</code> einsums — a domain-shape refusal, not dead space.</p><h2 id="the-pay-wall" tabindex="-1">The pay wall <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-pay-wall" aria-label="Permalink to “The pay wall”">​</a></h2><p>The driver admits every handler need (cumprod 3 laws, cumsum 8, logcumsumexp 1, scan_fold 2) but <strong>no atom pays</strong> (delta 0.0 on every corpus term):</p><ul><li><strong><code>scan_fold</code> — fire 0.</strong> Its only law that connects the atom to the corpus site, <code>sf.corpus_refold</code>, is <code>rejected-undeclarable</code> (<code>envs=164 eq=3 bad=1 real=1</code>): &quot;no declarable conjunction of &lt;= 3 covers 35 equal / 42 bad sites&quot;. The two certified laws (<code>sf.scale</code>, <code>sf.split_same</code>) are algebraic identities with no real sites, so nothing fires. This is the <strong>stabilization gap</strong>.</li><li><strong><code>cumsum</code> — fire 1, delta 0.</strong> One certified law (<code>cum.add_const</code>, the <code>cumsum(add(x, c))</code> shape) fires once on one corpus term, but its rewrite is cost-neutral: it does not lower the extracted FLOPs. <code>cumsum</code> is ambient (already bound), so minting it adds no extraction power either.</li></ul><h2 id="the-stabilization-gap-measured" tabindex="-1">The stabilization gap, measured <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-stabilization-gap-measured" aria-label="Permalink to “The stabilization gap, measured”">​</a></h2><p>The corpus SelectiveScan site is <code>mul(cumprod(sigmoid(A)), cumsum(B / clamp_min(cumprod(sigmoid(A)), 1e-6)))</code>; the minted atom is the <em>ideal</em> unclamped recurrence <code>fold_emit(sigmoid(A), B, 0.0, $acc, -2)</code>. Evaluating both in fp64 across a sweep of the gate magnitude:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>A-scale</th><th>min gate</th><th>clamp active</th><th>mint err</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1.0</td><td>1.34e-4</td><td>no</td><td>4.4e-16</td></tr><tr><td>5.0</td><td>3.17e-13</td><td>yes</td><td>2.57e+0</td></tr><tr><td>10.0</td><td>1.95e-25</td><td>yes</td><td>2.55e+0</td></tr><tr><td>30.0</td><td>8.07e-75</td><td>yes</td><td>3.09e+0</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The mint is exact while the cumulative gate stays above <code>1e-6</code> and diverges by O(1) the moment it underflows. The verification domain (<code>randn</code> A -&gt; sigmoid ~ 0.5, gate ~ 1e-4) sits in the inactive region, so the mint passes; the real site&#39;s gate underflows, so the recognition law is false there.</p><p><strong>Can the grammar express a stabilized fold? No — not as an affine recurrence.</strong> The clamp acts on the <em>accumulator</em> (the cumulative product), not on a fixed operand: the stabilized scan is a two-state, non-linear recurrence</p><pre><code>P_t = clamp_min(sigmoid(A_t) * P_{t-1}, eps)
S_t = S_{t-1} + B_t / P_t
out_t = P_t * S_t
</code></pre><p>whose state update is non-affine. The <code>fold</code>/<code>fold_emit</code> semantics is <code>acc = a_t * acc + b_t</code> with a_t, b_t fixed elementwise exprs; expressing the clamp needs a <strong>non-linear update function</strong> and a <strong>second coupled state</strong> — a semantics extension, not a vocabulary one. The atom must therefore stay ideal, and the corpus&#39;s clamped site is outside its reach.</p><h2 id="residue" tabindex="-1">Residue <a class="header-anchor" href="#residue" aria-label="Permalink to “Residue”">​</a></h2><ul><li>Stabilized (clamped) scans — a non-affine, two-state recurrence; the affine fold grammar cannot close it (above).</li><li><code>log_softmax</code> (a real invisible corpus op, 2 sites) — a normalization whose reduction result is wrapped in a unary (<code>log . sum . exp</code>) or a <code>logsumexp</code> reduction; the norm template covers a bare reduction operand only, and <code>logsumexp</code> has no torch binding.</li><li>Cost-neutral recognition: a certified law that fires without lowering extracted cost (the cumsum case) is an honest zero, not a bug — the atom&#39;s value would be its <em>execution</em>, which an ambient binding already provides.</li></ul>`,24)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};